.TH SDL_SetWindowSize 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetWindowSize \- Request that the size of a window\(aqs client area be set.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetWindowSize(SDL_Window *window, int w, int h);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the window is in a fullscreen or maximized state, this request has no effect\[char46]
.PP
To change the exclusive fullscreen mode of a window, use
.BR SDL_SetWindowFullscreenMode ()\[char46]
.PP
On some windowing systems, this request is asynchronous and the new window size may not have have been applied immediately upon the return of this function\[char46] If an immediate change is required, call
.BR SDL_SyncWindow ()
to block until the changes have taken effect\[char46]
.PP
When the window size changes, an
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_RESIZED
event will be emitted with the new window dimensions\[char46] Note that the new dimensions may not match the exact size requested, as some windowing systems can restrict the window size in certain scenarios (e\[char46]g\[char46] constraining the size of the content area to remain within the usable desktop bounds)\[char46] Additionally, as this is just a request, it can be denied by the windowing system\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window to change\[char46]
.TP
.I w
the width of the window, must be > 0\[char46]
.TP
.I h
the height of the window, must be > 0\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetWindowSize (3),
.BR SDL_SetWindowFullscreenMode (3),
.BR SDL_SyncWindow (3)
